<title>USA: First Palm Beach Q4 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>First Palm Beach Q4 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PALM BEACH, Fla. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.97   profit	 $0.36</p>
<p> Net loss		   4,940   profit	 1,870</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.58   profit	 $1.11</p>
<p> Net profit		 2,949   profit	 5,646</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name Is First Palm Beach Bancorp Inc.</p>
<p>Current quarter includes one-time SAIF after-tax charge of $4.0 million, or $0.78 a share.</p>
<p>During the current quarter, the company recorded a provision for loan losses of $8.9 million, primarily due to indirect automobile lending, which included additional loss reserves of $5.4 million, to cover anticipated losses related to indirect lending portfolio.</p>
<p>A net gain of $3.5 million on sale of loans was recorded during the current quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
